30,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The minutes show no review of the current arrangement in five years. It’s stagnant.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"The sticker register shows some flats have three bikes, others none. Demand is uneven.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,I watched four mornings. Eleven bikes leave between 7 and 9. Shoving is constant.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The ledger is thin. Capital work needs a levy. The ward park charges 2,600 yen.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The treasurer spends three hours a month on cash. Adding billing will double that.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, three hours is a lot. Who takes that on?","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,The rain exposure is bad past the downpipe. Saddles stay wet.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, that matches what I saw. People are frustrated by the wet spots.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"If we charge, it must be less than 2,600 yen to be competitive.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,The complaint log has nine entries. All died out because no one owned the problem.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,The lack of ownership is the real issue. A paid system might create that.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"But if people can’t pay, they’ll resent it. The sticker data shows varied needs.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"A lottery might be fair, but it ignores the morning rush reality.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,Shared racks avoid the billing headache. But do they solve the shoving?,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,Shared racks mean no individual accountability. The complaints will just continue.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I’m leaning towards a system that assigns responsibility.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I worry about the social cost of a lottery.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,The physical layout needs fixing regardless of the rule.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,Let’s look at the options. We have enough data to judge.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I agree. The maintenance burden is the deciding factor for me.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option A, Paid Allocation, creates a clear owner for each space.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Option B, Annual Lottery, feels arbitrary. It doesn’t address the morning rush.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C, Shared Racks, might reduce the shoving if the racks are good.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option A generates income. The ledger shows we need it for capital work.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option A adds billing work. But it solves the accountability issue.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, the income is useful, but the social risk is high.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,I prefer C. It’s open and avoids the resentment of a lottery.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"C is risky. If the racks are bad, the shoving gets worse.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,A is the most sustainable financially. The ward park proves people will pay.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,A is the only one that assigns clear responsibility. I support it.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I’m concerned about the arrears in the neighbouring block.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,But the sticker register says people would rather pay than be equal.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,That’s a strong point. People value certainty.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,Certainty is worth the administrative cost. I vote A.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,The maintenance burden is manageable if we rotate the treasurer.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"I’ll vote A, but we need a clear payment plan.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I’ll vote C. I can’t support a system that might exclude people.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I’ll vote A. The morning rush needs a solution, not just a lottery.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,A is the rational choice.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Toshio,,A is the practical choice.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
